==Strategy==
With a titanic '''3 million''' HP, fast attacks, Omni-Strike and strong DPS, the guardian of the ancient realm pulls no punches. You might notice similarities between Relic Bun-Bun and [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Mecha-Bun]]. However, while Relic Bun-Bun has much less DPS and speed, it does not have the Floating trait. This throws the strategy of stacking Necro-Dancer cats out of the window, and makes Relic Bun-Bun much more challenging to fight than its counterpart.

Relic Bun-Bun might seem unbeatable, but true to [[Relic Bun-Bun#EN|the prophecies]], there are a selection of cats who can quell its rampage. Here are the non-Uber counters to Relic Bun-Bun and their obtainment methods:
*The [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]] [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] True Forms are the intended counter for this ancient contraption. They all possess respectable anti-Relic abilities that make them great additions to any team.
*If one has [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], they can use [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] to control the Relic Doge flow, allowing them to be stalled in Cyberpunk's blindspot. This allows you to build a stack of Cyberpunk Cats to permanently Slow Relic Bun-Bun. This method does not demand any NP investment, though it is time consuming. Should you have [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]], even better.
*[[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]], with his Target Relic talent, and [[Medusa Cat (Rare Cat)|Medusa Cat]], obtained from beating Masked Okame, can stall Relic Bun-Bun with their Slow and Freeze procs, respectively. Furthermore, both of them can also be used to defeat Primeval Cyclone and unlock [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]], a meatshield that can stall Relic Bun-Bun very effectively. While Medusa Cat is much less consistent and harder to use, she does not require any NP investment.
*Should one have [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]], they can use him to defeat Primeval Cyclone, therefore unlocking Modern Cat and being able to defeat Relic Bun-Bun.
*[[Good-Luck Ebisu (Super Rare Cat)|Bad-Luck Ebisu]] is hard to obtain as a limited unit, but he can be put to great use. By stacking him in the startoff, he can repeatedly harass Relic Bun-Bun with a stream of debuffs, helping control it.

Alongside these options, [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] can help provide a consistent source of damage output. [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] works well in conjunction with Modern Cat, helping stall Relic Bun-Bun further. A Level '''20+61''' [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and a Level '''40''' [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] can survive two hits from Relic Bun-Bun, which can be useful.

On 2-Crown and 3-Crown difficulties of the stage, Relic Bun-Bun gains much higher magnifications and has gargantuan stats as a result, and the Relic Doges become even more annoying. However, by this point you would already have stronger anti-Relic options like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]] and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]], making the stage manageable.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Support [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] with freeze or slow can be very useful for this level. These can be especially good for covering Cyberpunk's blindspot.

*[[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]]: Very useful for this level and will be able to work very well with Cyberpunk. His [[Freeze]] added with [[Weaken]] can allow your units to have a bit of recovery once the Freeze wears off. However, you must stack Piccolans on the first Relic Doges, otherwise Piccolan's low uptime will render it useless; note that it takes 300 seconds to spawn a new Piccolan, so bring a Speed Up.
*[[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan]]: Can be used in similar way is Piccolan, for the purpose of covering Cyberpunk Cat's blind spot. Not only does he have the longest standing range in the game, but his attack rate is significantly faster than Piccolan. His [[Slow]] ability can also extend upon Cyberpunk's effect and with Cyberstacking could theoretically perma-Slow. Also similar to Piccolan, Assassinlan's cooldown is painfully long to stack, so bring a Speed Up.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]]: With his [[Immune to Curse]] and Target Relic talents, Gravolodon can hold the frontline for a while, though this requires a good bit of NP investment.
*[[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]]: While Mitama's Slow has very high uptime, the amount that she outranges Relic Bun-Bun's [[Omni Strike]] by is low, and, once [[Curse]]d, she's incapacitated for quite some time. With the help of Cyberpunk Cat and/or Sniper The Deadeye and Talented Rodeo Cat she can make the Relic Bun-Bun never move again.
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Chronos the Infinite]]: Chronos has Freeze, which is more helpful to keep meatshields alive and has higher standing range, so she isn't as risky to bring on, as well as lower cost; however, her uptime is lower.
*[[D'artanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Meow-sketeer]]: Meow-sketeer just barely outranges the Bun Bun's Omni, but if you can establish a strong frontline defense, he'll be able to shred it without having to worry about being cursed.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Daybreaker Izanagi]]: With minimal peons on this stage, Izanagi's [[Insane Damage]] and [[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]] will help despite his Single Attack. His [[Conjure]] can be used to clear peons or get Relic Bun-Bun off of him if it pushes too hard, and Izanagi outranges Bun-Bun, even when accounting for his Omni Strike.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Squire Luno]]: With his beefy health against Relics, he can soak up quite a few hits from Relic Bun-Bun for his measly 900 cent cost. His [[Conjure]] being able to push back Relic Bun-Bun works perfectly with Sniperpunk stacking, as it can keep Relic Bun-Bun pinned to the base with an almost 100% uptime when paired with a Sniperpunk stack. His [[Mini-Surge]] can also provide chip damage and stall Relic Bun-Bun and Relic Doges, effectively never letting Relic Bun-Bun move into Cyberpunk's blindspot.
*Talented [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]]: With her Target Relic and Curse Immunity Talents, she becomes a decent tank to stall for time as your other big units recharge and is also capable of weakening the boss.
*Talented [[Trickster Himeyuri (Uber Rare Cat)|Fox Queen Himeyuri]]: While this does require quite a bit of Talent investment, Himeyuri can reliably get 70% uptime on her slow against Relic Bun-Bun, which can be increased with Slow Up Cat Combos. She can also reposition 4 times with her knockbacks, and does a respectable amount of damage if all of her attacks hit.
*Talented [[Detective Vigler (Uber Rare Cat)|Section Chief Gravicci]]: While this also requires NP, it is more than worth it, as Gravicci can Freeze Relic Bun-Bun and is immune to his Curses, with their Wave also freezing Relic Doge. This unit is also good for most of UL in general.

